IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nba-types`

-- Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK) — GOAL 2: ARTICLE 31(1) IMMUNITY
-- FROM PENALTIES (s 37).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2022-36.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — Article 31(1) immunity`

-- s 37(1) "A refugee is not to be taken to have come to the United Kingdom
-- directly from a country where their life or freedom was threatened if, in
-- coming from that country, they stopped in another country outside the
-- United Kingdom, unless they can show that they could not reasonably be
-- expected to have sought protection under the Refugee Convention in that
-- country."
@ref s 37(1)
GIVEN f IS AN `Article 31 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refugee came directly under` f IF
        NOT (f's `stopped in another country on the way`)
    OR  f's `could not reasonably have sought protection there`

-- s 37(2) "A refugee is not to be taken to have presented themselves without
-- delay to the authorities unless— (a) [if they became a refugee outside the
-- UK] they made a claim for asylum as soon as reasonably practicable after
-- their arrival ...; (b) [if inside] (i) if their presence ... was lawful at
-- that time, they made a claim ... before ... their presence ... became
-- unlawful; (ii) if ... unlawful at that time, ... as soon as reasonably
-- practicable after they became aware of their need for protection".
@ref s 37(2)-(3)
GIVEN f IS AN `Article 31 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refugee presented themselves without delay under` f IF
    IF   f's `became a refugee while outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN f's `claimed as soon as reasonably practicable after arrival`
    ELSE IF   f's `presence in the UK was lawful when they became a refugee`
         THEN f's `claimed before their presence became unlawful`
         ELSE f's `claimed as soon as reasonably practicable after becoming aware of the need`

-- s 37(4) "A penalty is not to be taken as having been imposed on account of
-- a refugee's illegal entry or presence ... where the penalty relates to
-- anything done by the refugee in the course of an attempt to leave the
-- United Kingdom."
@ref s 37(1)-(4)
@export Whether the conditions in s 37 of the Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK) for Article 31(1) immunity from penalties are met for a refugee: they came directly (no stop in another country, unless they could not reasonably have sought protection there), presented themselves without delay (as s 37(2) defines it), and the penalty does not relate to an attempt to leave the United Kingdom. Article 31's own requirement of good cause is not covered. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS AN `Article 31 facts`  @desc The journey, when they became a refugee, their status then, when they claimed, and what the penalty relates to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 37 conditions for Article 31(1) immunity are met by` f IF
        `the refugee came directly under` f
    AND `the refugee presented themselves without delay under` f
    AND NOT (f's `the penalty relates to an attempt to leave the UK`)
